Spec: SystemContextScript

Platform: Rhai script library (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine)

Purpose:
  The system-kind context orchestrator: structural twin of ./../service/context.rhai
    (./../service/context.sdd) and ./../tenant/context.rhai (./../tenant/context.sdd),
    one level above @build_context. It delegates the whole assembly to `build_context`
    and drives named hook slots, nothing more — the purest of the three orchestrators:
    it reads no `instance` property, no `args` key, and no engine surface of its own
    beyond the hook shims. Deltas from the twins: it overlays `template_dir` and
    `agent_image` on neither lane (no system Rust lane carries those flags), it mints
    no kind block at all — no `namespace`, no `tenant`, hence no
    `maintenance_start_hour`/`maintenance_start_minut` pair anywhere on the system
    contract — the kind slot is `context_system` whose shipped default
    ./context_system.rhai is an identity, and the offline chain stops at
    `context_post` — `context_after` never resolving offline, the tenant-twin
    asymmetry the service twin does not have.

Exposes:
  @run(@instance, @args) — live lane, the entry point the agent system `install` and
    `delete` Rust snippets call as `import("context") as ctx; ctx::run(instance, args)`
    (/agent/src/system/install.sdd, /agent/src/system/delete.sdd; also the
    @ENTRY_POINT_FUNCTIONS lint name `run` of /agent/src/linting/rhai_checker.sdd);
    delegates to `build::run`, invokes the five hooks through the three-arg
    @import_run.
  @template(@instance, @args) — offline twin for `agent template system`: delegates to
    `build::template`, hooks through three-arg @import_template, four slots only —
    `context_after` is never resolved here.
  No other @fn exists — importing this module (alias convention `as ctx`, also under
    the package-shadow name `context`) exposes exactly these two.

Accepts:
  @instance — forwarded only, never property-read and never method-called here (the
    tenant twin's inline identity reads have no system counterpart). Callers inject:
    the typed @SystemInstance @Dynamic fetched by @SystemInstance::get before the eval
    (/agent/src/system/install.sdd, /agent/src/system/delete.sdd), the synthesized
    `#{metadata: {name, namespace}}` map of the offline lane
    (/agent/src/template/system.sdd), or the mock-sink value reached under registered
    name @get_system_instance in `agent package test` (/agent/src/testing/handler.sdd).
  @args — plain map, read by zero key in this file (both twins read two keys here —
    delta): install lane the eight snake_case keys of the serialized @Parameters
    (`namespace`, `instance`, `vynil_namespace`, `package_dir`, `script_dir`, `tag`,
    `config_dir`, `controller_values`); delete lane the same minus `tag`, so
    `instance.requested` lands `()` from the delegation upstream (tolerated map-miss —
    the delete-stage scripts never index it, while ./install.rhai closes the install
    lane through `context.instance.requested`); template lane the nine keys of
    /agent/src/template/system.sdd (@Parameters adds `context_name`). NO system lane's
    @Parameters carries `template_dir` or `agent_image` — the @clap fields the
    service/tenant twins drop are absent from the system shape, not merely unread.
    Everything is consumed downstream through the delegation and the hooks (read
    contract ./../lib/build_context.sdd).

Returns:
  The context map (last expression; the calling snippet passes it as the second
    argument to `install::run`/`delete::run`, and the Rust lane discards the snippet
    @Dynamic). Stock insertion order of top-level keys, both lanes identical:
    1. the delegate's seven: `cluster`, `controller`, `instance`, `values`, `defaults`,
        `package_dir`, `config_dir` (key contract owned by ./../lib/build_context.sdd
        Returns),
    2. whatever the `context_pre` replacement leaves (whole-map replacement can rewrite
        or erase every key above),
    3. `extra` — always written to the `context_extra` result, no guard; the stock
        image (no such module ships) stores `()` under the key.
    `context_post` (both lanes) and `context_after` (run lane only) may then rebind the
    whole map again. Eight stock keys — the service stock had eleven because it also
    minted `template_dir`/`agent_image`/`namespace`; a system context NEVER shows
    those three keys unless a hook injects them, and a `context.namespace...` read in
    a package script ported from the twin lanes then gets the tolerant-map-miss `()`
    downstream, not an error here. Later stage modules of the same run add keys (e.g.
    ./install_tofu.rhai's `tofu`); that is their contract.

Raises:
  Zero @throw statement, zero @try, zero guard of its own:
    - Delegation errors land whole (package.yaml read, agent.yaml YAML, unguarded
      cluster reads per ./../lib/build_context.sdd Raises).
    - Hook errors: @import_run/@import_template swallow ONLY absent-module /
      absent-function (skip with @log_debug, semantics owned by wynil-core
      @add_common); anything a hook throws for real propagates through `throw ;` and
      aborts the lane run — surfaced per lane as @common::Error::Core exiting
      install `1`, delete `3`, template `3` (/agent/src/system/install.sdd,
      /agent/src/system/delete.sdd, /agent/src/template/system.sdd Err lanes).
    - A hook that returns a map lacking a later-read key is NOT an error here — the
      property read fails downstream in the consuming stage.

Handles:
  Stock image hook posture: only the kind slot `context_system` ships (this
    directory); `context_pre`/`context_extra`/`context_post`/`context_after` skip on
    every lane to `()` so the `type_of` guards keep the running context and only
    `extra` changes (to `()`). The shipped kind slot keeps the map identical
    (./context_system.rhai identity).
  Non-map hook return (including the skip `()`) silently keeps the previous context —
    the guard is `type_of(ctx) == "map"`, whole-value replacement, no key merge.
  @import_template fallback: a hook module without a `template` fn but with a `run` is
    invoked at `run(instance, context)` on the offline lane — the shipped
    ./context_system.rhai is the built-in example, its identity is exactly how the
    system template lane passes its kind slot.
  Delete-lane missing `tag`: tolerated map-miss upstream, `()` flows on.
  Package shadow resolution: the calling lanes search `{package_dir}/scripts`,
    `{config_dir}`, `{script_dir}/system`, `{script_dir}/lib` in order — a package
    `context.rhai` replaces this whole orchestrator, a package `context_system.rhai`
    replaces just the kind slot ahead of the identity default, and a package
    `build_context.rhai` replaces the delegate this file imports plainly.

Must:
  Keep the module body at one plain `import "build_context" as build` plus the two
    `fn` declarations — no top-level statement runs at import; both entry names match
    @ENTRY_POINT_FUNCTIONS.
  Run the two lanes in this order, each guarded slot exactly once: delegate into
    `build::run` (or `build::template`) whole; slot `context_pre`; slot
    `context_system`; write `context["extra"]` from slot `context_extra`; slot
    `context_post`; then [run lane only] slot `context_after`; then return `context`.
  Hand the hook the running context as third argument: @import_run("context_pre",
    @instance, @context) on the live lane, @import_template("context_pre", @instance,
    @context) on the offline lane — always the three-arg shims, so wynil-core resolves
    the 3-arg overloads.
  Replace the context on the pre/system/post/after slots through the
    `type_of(ctx) == "map"` guard, whole map, no key merge; write `extra` unguarded
    from the slot result (any value, including `()`, becomes the stored value).
  Mint nothing but `extra`: `extra` is the only key this file writes; `template_dir`,
    `agent_image`, `namespace` and `tenant` are never stored here on either lane.
  Touch nothing: zero k8s/file/http engine calls, zero property reads of @instance or
    @args in these 42 source lines; every read lives behind the delegation
    (./../lib/build_context.sdd Handles) or a resolved hook.
  Preserve the key spelling `extra` — its one shipped consumer is ./install_tofu.rhai
    calling @tfg::gen_files, whose @gen_locals renders `context.extra` into the
    `vynil_extra` local of `00_vynil_locals.tf` (/agent/scripts/lib/tofu_gen.sdd); no
    other script under this directory reads `context.extra` directly.

Must not:
  Re-sync onto the twin lanes by adding a `namespace`/maintenance mint or a
    `template_dir`/`agent_image` overlay: the system contract is keyless-by-design on
    all three keys (Accepts/Returns, decision frozen-open in
    /agent/src/template/system.sdd Tasks), and nothing under this directory reads a
    maintenance pair (the system kind ships no backup/restore lane at all).

Depends on:
  ./../lib/build_context.rhai — the whole delegation (frozen in
    ./../lib/build_context.sdd; only the seam — call once, per lane, first — is this
    file's contract).
  ./context_system.rhai — the one shipped hook slot; slot placement only here, the
    identity itself in ./context_system.sdd.
  wynil-core 0.7.7 script surface (@Script `add_common` behind
    /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd): three-arg @import_run and @import_template with the
    four-overload family and the absent-`template` run-fallback, @type_of, plain module
    `import` name resolution.
  Counterpart contracts, call edges flow the other way (they import this module):
    /agent/src/system/install.sdd and /agent/src/system/delete.sdd (live `ctx::run`),
    /agent/src/template/system.sdd (offline `ctx::template`),
    /agent/src/testing/handler.sdd (mock-engine lane of `agent package test`).

References:
  ./../service/context.sdd and ./../tenant/context.sdd — the twin specs. The
    three-way diff: only this file skips the `template_dir`/`agent_image` overlay and
    the kind mint; service's own References paragraph ("neither mints
    template_dir/agent_image") is true of this file and already corrected FALSE for
    tenant in ./../tenant/context.sdd; its "both twins call `context_after` only on
    the live lane" claim is true of both twins (this file's offline stop verified
    against source).
  /agent/src/template/system.sdd — the Rust lane that freezes this file's behaviour
    from its side: no hardcoded kind block, chain stops at `context_post`, keyless
    args.
  /agent/scripts/lib/tofu_gen.sdd — the `vynil_extra` consumer of `extra`.
  /agent/src/linting/rhai_checker.sdd — the `run`/`template` entry-name lint.

Scenario: stock live lane assembles with the identity kind slot
  Given a mock engine resolving the `scripts/system` and `scripts/lib` dirs, no
    package-side hook modules, a mocked @SystemInstance
  When @run(@instance, @args) executes
  Then the delegate's seven keys exist in order, `context_system` runs its identity
    `run` and the guarded replace keeps the identical map, the four absent hooks
    @log_debug their skip lines, `extra` is `()` as a present key, eight top-level
    keys come back, and no `namespace`/`template_dir`/`agent_image` key was added
  No mapped test

Scenario: offline lane mirrors the sequence and stops at context_post
  Given the /agent/src/template/system.sdd synthesized `#{metadata: {name,
    namespace}}` and the nine template-lane args
  When @template(@instance, @args) executes
  Then the four slots run via the template shim in pre → system → extra → post order,
    the kind slot is reached through the absent-`template` run-fallback, a package
    `context_after` module is never resolved offline, and the map carries no
    kind-block key
  No mapped test

Scenario: a hook returning a map replaces everything
  Given a hook module (package `context_pre`) whose callable returns `#{only: 1}`
  When a guarded slot takes it
  Then the context becomes `#{only: 1}` (delegate keys erased), after which this file
    still writes `extra` onto it — consumers reading erased keys get `()` downstream,
    not an error here
  No mapped test

Scenario: a package shadows the identity kind slot
  Given `${package_dir}/scripts/context_system.rhai` returning a map that adds a
    `kind` block ahead of the shipped default
  When a lane slot resolves `context_system`
  Then the package copy wins the resolver order, its guarded map replacement takes
    over, and later slots see its output
  No mapped test

Tasks:
  [ ] Map the scenarios: /agent/tests/rhai_lifecycle.rs builds service engines only
      (`make_service_script` over `scripts/service` + `scripts/lib`); add a
      system-lane resolver builder plus a fixture packages dir so hook shadowing and
      the run-fallback are testable before the TTD green gate.
  [?] Keyless-lane confirmation: no system lane ever sees `template_dir` or
      `agent_image` (Rust @Parameters drops them AND this file overlays nothing), so
      tooling ported from the twin data contract reads `()` — mirror the
      deliberately-keyless-vs-restore decision open in
      /agent/src/template/system.sdd Tasks and the three-leaf @Parameters
      unification there.
  [?] Kind-block absence as contract: no system context carries a maintenance pair
      and nothing under this directory reads one (no system backup/restore lane
      exists to consume it, unlike the twins' ./../lib/backup_context.rhai cron).
      Confirm the absence is deliberate and permanent, not pending backup support.
  [?] `extra` unguarded and whole-map replacement semantics: same open decisions as
      ./../service/context.sdd and ./../tenant/context.sdd Tasks — decide once for
      all three lanes.
  [?] `context_after` offline absence: the live-only asymmetry this file shares with
      the tenant twin (service fires it on both lanes) — resolve together with
      ./../tenant/context.sdd's twin-drift task and a unified slot set.

Done when:
  Every Scenario has a mock-engine test or a decided Task, the three-way twin diff
    above still matches all three sources, the key claims cross-check
    ./../lib/build_context.sdd, ./context_system.sdd and
    /agent/src/template/system.sdd, and `specdd lint` is green.
